/scenes/Test_CodeEdit.gd\", \"res://text_test/test_script.gd\"]`\nAnd it returns an empty array when all are saved.\n\nIn certain edge cases, it is possible to get a completely unsaved script open which results in an output like `[\"\", \"::4sao5\"]`. It's technically correct to return them and should be distinguished from the case when all are saved so its good. Absolute paths may be returned too, if the file is outside of the project. Users may have to account for these depending on the use case.","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113762#pullrequestreview-3977640394","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/113762","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","submitted_at":"2026-03-19T19:57:44Z"}]